# Frontend architecture (FSD + Next.js)

**Feature-Sliced Design** with Next.js-oriented naming. Conventions below apply to the **app source root** (the directory that contains the Next.js `app` router tree and FSD layers).

## Layer mapping (Next.js vs classic FSD)

**Layers** (FSD names, top → bottom of the import graph): **`app`**, **`pages`**, **`widgets`**, **`features`**, **`entities`**, **`shared`**. Do not use **`processes`**—it is deprecated in current FSD. Add only the layers your product needs. Here **`application`** = **`app`**, **`views`** = **`pages`**; **`widgets`**, **`features`**, **`entities`**, **`shared`** keep FSD folder names.

- **Classic `app` → this project `application`**: bootstrap layer (global styles, providers, shells, document/layout glue, translations), not routable page UI.
- **Classic `pages` → this project `views`**: route-level UI and slice `model`, composed from thin App Router entry files.
- **Next.js `app` routes**: keep route modules (`page`, `layout`, …) minimal in **`*.tsx`** and import screen UI from the **`views`** layer via path alias.

## Slices and segments

- **Slice** = one business vertical: `<layer>/<sliceName>/` (e.g. a product area under **`views`**, a chrome block under **`widgets`**, a domain object under **`entities`**).
- **Segments**: FSD defines five—**`ui`**, **`model`**, **`lib`**, **`api`**, **`config`**; use only those a slice needs.
- **Public API**: each slice exposes a root **`index.ts`** (barrel). Prefer path aliases: `@/<layer>/<slice>/...` (configure alias root to match the repo).

## `views` (replaces classic “pages”)

- Primary screen UI lives in **`ui`** (top-level component file or folder when styles/parts are needed).
- **`subpages`**: nested routes get a folder under **`ui/subpages/<kebab-case>/`** per nested URL segment.
- **`model`** segment: slice-specific schemas, constants, utils, mocks, interfaces—grouped by **kind** (see [Grouping by kind inside segments](#grouping-by-kind-inside-segments)).

## `application` (name for the FSD “app” layer)

- Global **styles**, **providers**, **shells**, **document** wrappers, **i18n** message bundles—no routable page UI here; that stays in **`views`**.

## `ui` and `parts` (widgets, entities, shared UI)

- The main component for a folder may sit next to **`*.module.scss`** (e.g. a **PascalCase** folder whose primary file is matching **`*.tsx`**).
- **Subcomponents** live in **`parts/`** beside that UI.
- **`parts/index.ts`**: re-export all part modules.
- **Part with own styles**: use a **PascalCase subfolder** containing the part component + its `*.module.scss`—avoid a loose `*.module.scss` next to a flat part file under `parts/`.
- **No nested `parts`**: do not add `parts/.../parts/`; split into siblings or lift to parent `ui`.

## Grouping by kind inside segments

In **segments** that hold slice-local TypeScript (typically **`model`**, **`lib`**, **`config`**—see *Slices and segments* above), group files by **kind** into subfolders, each with an **`index.ts`** barrel—even for a single file of that kind.

**Kind** subfolder names and matching **role suffixes** on **`*.ts`** / **`*.tsx`** (the dot-segment before the final extension) are defined by **`front/eslint.config.js`**: rule **`simple-import-sort/imports`** → **`groups`**.

After the `@/` alias groups:
- **`hooks`** is its own group (`\\/hooks$` plus **`use*`** basename patterns).
- The following groups pair a **folder** pattern (`\\/segment$`) with a **file** pattern (`\\.role$` before **`*.ts`**); use that pairing and order as canonical.

Not in those groups but used in this repo: **`atoms/`** with **`*.atom.ts`** (Jotai), and **`*.test.ts`** for unit tests.

## File naming: sub-extensions

- **Components** (`*.tsx` **without** a role suffix per [Grouping by kind inside segments](#grouping-by-kind-inside-segments)): **no** dot-style suffix; use **PascalCase** consistent with the main export. Any **`*.tsx`** with a role suffix is **Other kinds**, not this bullet.
- **Hooks** (`*.ts` / **`*.tsx`**): **no** dot-style role suffix; file name is **`use` + PascalCase** (the `use` prefix is required for hooks).
- **Other kinds**: **dot suffix** + folder as in [Grouping by kind inside segments](#grouping-by-kind-inside-segments) (and the **`atoms`** / **`*.test.ts`** note).

## Folder and file casing

- **App Router** URL segments and **`views/.../subpages/`** paths: **kebab-case** (e.g. `feature-name`, `parent-segment/nested-segment`).
- **React component** folders and files: **PascalCase**; primary **`*.tsx`** has **no** role suffix and matches the main export basename.
- **Non-component** folders and role-suffixed **`*.ts`** / **`*.tsx`**: **lowerCamelCase**; segment folder names and suffix pairing—[Grouping by kind inside segments](#grouping-by-kind-inside-segments).

## Next.js routes vs `views`

- **`app/**/page` (`*.tsx`)**: keep thin—locale, metadata, framework setup, then render from **`views`** (or equivalent alias).
- **Shared page prop types** and cross-route types: **`shared/model`** (or your shared types layer), not **`application`**.

## Cross-cutting notes

- **i18n routing/config**: keep a small dedicated module; do not mix heavy domain logic into it.
- Prefer **absolute imports** via the configured path alias.
- New slices should **mirror** an existing slice’s **segments** (e.g. **`ui`**, **`model`**) and public **`index.ts`** layout rather than inventing a one-off structure.
